      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    face_value = 100_000\n    coupon_rate = 0.05\n    initial_market_rate = coupon_rate\n    new_market_rate = 0.06\n    years_to_maturity = 10\n\n    # Calculate the bond price at each market rate\n    annual_coupon = face_value * coupon_rate\n\n    initial_price = sum(\n        annual_coupon / ((1 + initial_market_rate) ** year)\n        for year in range(1, years_to_maturity + 1)\n    ) + face_value / ((1 + initial_market_rate) ** years_to_maturity)\n\n    new_price = sum(\n        annual_coupon / ((1 + new_market_rate) ** year)\n        for year in range(1, years_to_maturity + 1)\n    ) + face_value / ((1 + new_market_rate) ** years_to_maturity)\n\n    # Calculate percentage price change\n    percentage_change = ((new_price - initial_price) / initial_price) * 100\n\n    # Return the percentage change rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(percentage_change, 2)\n```",
